---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import NextProject from '../../components/NextProject.astro';
---
<Base title="LogRite · Tejitha Kristem" description="LogRite: the marketing website for Deployd's in-house AI-governance platform." calm>
  <article style="--accent: #E2562A">
    <header class="cs-head">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="back" href="/projects"><span class="arr">←</span> All projects</a>
        <span class="eyebrow mono">Website design · Framer</span>
        <h1 class="cs-title">Log<span class="accent">Rite</span></h1>
        <p class="cs-sub">AI governance for AI tools, made <span class="hl">easy to get at first read.</span></p>
        <ul class="chips">
          <li class="live">● Live site</li>
          <li>Deployd in-house product</li>
          <li>Framer</li>
        </ul>
        <dl class="tldr">
          <div><dt class="mono">What it is</dt><dd>Deployd's in-house AI-governance platform, built for B2B teams</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mono">Who it's for</dt><dd>Compliance leads and engineering teams in regulated industries</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mono">My role</dt><dd>Joined after launch to design the marketing website, plus content and SEO</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mono">Pages</dt><dd>Homepage, plus pages for each product and audience</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 28px">
          <p>LogRite is Deployd's own product: AI governance for AI tools. It sets the rules your code, AI models and AI agents should follow, and logs everything they do against those rules, so teams can prove it. Our team built it for other companies, especially in regulated industries like federal and fintech.</p>
          <p>I came in after the product launched. Since it's our own product, we wanted a marketing website as good as the platform, so <strong>I took it up</strong>: the homepage and dedicated pages for each product and audience, designed in Framer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-hero-img rise"><img src="/images/logrite-hero.webp" alt="LogRite homepage hero: The governance layer for everything you run. Your code, your models, your agents." width="1100" height="619" /></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">01 · Scope</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">The core <em>design challenge</em></h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>AI governance across code, models and agents is hard to picture. And a compliance lead reads a page very differently from an engineering lead. <strong>The site couldn't flatten both into generic SaaS speak.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <div class="boxes" style="--cols: 2">
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Reader 1</span><h3>The compliance buyer</h3><p>Needs to see the rules enforced and the evidence stored, in plain language.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Reader 2</span><h3>The engineering lead</h3><p>Needs to see how it plugs into code, API calls and agents without slowing anyone down.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">02 · Analytics & marketing</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">Beyond <em>the screens</em></h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>I stayed on past launch. I wrote LinkedIn content built from the site's own messaging, and worked in Google Analytics and Search Console to fix indexing issues: pages crawled but not indexed, 404s and robots.txt blocks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="boxes">
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Content</span><h3>LinkedIn posts</h3><p>Built from the site's messaging, so the story stays consistent.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Search</span><h3>Indexing fixes</h3><p>Crawled-not-indexed pages, 404s and robots.txt blocks.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Analytics</span><h3>GA + Search Console</h3><p>Watching how people actually find and use the site.</p></div>
        </div>
        <NextProject current="logrite" />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
